**Consequence:** this project's Terraform state lives in the S3 bucket shared
across every project generated from this template, keyed
`{{ project_slug }}/<environment>/terraform.tfstate` — not a bucket this
project owns or manages. Isolation from other projects in the bucket is this
project's deploy role, scoped to its own `{{ project_slug }}/*` prefix. See
`terraform/README.md`.
**Consequence:** deploys go through `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`, which
sequences the stages in `.github/actions/` — see `docs/deploy.md`. Any deploy
step this project needs that the template doesn't have is a new stage there,
gated on the capability that owns it, with its own test.
