## Staging starts with no data
**Context:** the `seed` deploy stage reseeds staging from production, and this
project's production data is real.
**Decision:** it copies nothing until `scripts/sanitize-seed.js` exists here.
**Why:** the template cannot know which of this project's attributes are
personal data, so it refuses rather than guessing. Writing that sanitizer —
and deciding what staging is allowed to know — is a decision this project owes
its own entry for, above this line, when it makes it.
**Consequence:** until then an empty staging table is the expected state, not
a bug. Start from `scripts/sanitize-seed.example.js`.
{% endif %}
